# legs/adult/loco/std: the adult legs in trousers and boots, shared by the man and the woman (regions: T thigh, K knee, S shin, B boot, O sole)
# The slice (P2b wave 1, FOLK-BODY); A3's pixels are the reference (docs/ref/style_a3). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# ROLLOUT ADULT-RIG polish (2026-10-22): run3 / run6 (flight, base and woman) the thighs separate below the seat: on row
# y -9 each thigh ends on its own outline with a pixel of grass between them (run3: the trailing near thigh u -3..0, no lit
# pixel past its outline; run6: the lead near thigh starts on an outline at u +3); far.pxm's run6 trailing thigh likewise.
# RUN FIX i3 (2026-10-22; the blind panel on i2: the contact's trailing leg knelt, its shin level at ankle height and
# its boot a flat brick hanging a pixel off the ground; the push's support leg a straight stilt). CONTACT (run1 / run4):
# the TRAILING leg (the one that just pushed off) hangs from the hip, the knee under the seat, the shin running down and
# back at about 45 degrees (rows 5, 6, 6 wide: the full thickness across the bone) into K3 toe-down, its toe 2 px off the
# ground behind the planted heel (RESEARCH 5.3: "trailing, sole 2 px up, toe down"), no level shin, no kneel. PUSH (run2 /
# run5): the support leg gives at the knee (the thigh steeper, the knee row a pixel forward: bend about 20 degrees) while
# it still leans back 30 degrees onto its toe. FLIGHT as i2.
# RUN FIX i2 (2026-10-22; the blind panel on i1: the flight's trailing leg read as a thigh held level behind the seat,
# the lead boot as a flat slab hovering, the contact knee as a post). FLIGHT (run3 / run6): the TRAILING thigh drops
# straight down three rows inside the hem span, the knee breaks back under the seat, and the shin runs down and back into
# K9 (the library's pointed trailing foot: toe down and back along the shin, heel up at the ankle), its toe 3 px off the
# ground; the LEAD keeps i1's driven knee and hanging shin, the boot K1 toe-up (reaching for the heel strike) 3 px up.
# CONTACT (run1 / run4): the landing knee a pixel prouder (the knee row u 2..6, the thigh row above it widened forward).
# THE RUN, RUN FIX i1 (2026-10-22; the owner on proto6 i3: approved, then: use the run's newly allowed 2 px bob for a real
# moment in the air, even the contact's long hold, a bent landing knee). run1 / run4 (contact) and run3 / run6 (flight)
# redrawn, hand-placed; run2 / run5 (push) are proto6 i2's a pixel forward (the support's toe at u -1, heel -6):
#   FLIGHT (the open scissor, kept; loco.clip bob -2): both legs start a row higher under the raised hem (the seat row
#     y-11); the LEAD thigh forward out of the hips' front half, the knee driven up and forward (u +8), the shin hanging
#     straight under it into the flat K0 3 rows up (its whole 20 px drawing, nothing over it); the TRAILING thigh down
#     inside the coat, the knee behind it, the shin angled down and back (2 px a row, never a level bar) into K3 3 rows up
#     (heel up behind, toe down: the foot that just pushed off), the boot whole under the shin; grass under both boots.
#   CONTACT: the landing foot flat at u 0 (a pixel further under the body: the contact holds 6 px, not 8), the knee bent
#     3 px proud of the ankle (the thigh forward a pixel a row, the shin back); the other leg folding through behind as
#     proto6 i1's.
# Superseded where it differs (PROTO6 i2):
