# History, superseded where it differs by proto2 i3 above:
# THE SIDE RUN, PROTO2 i2 (2026-10-21; the blind panel on i1: "a fast walk", no airborne frame, the front leg locked
# straight in flight, the recover boots lumped; supersedes i1's run below; i1's walk is unchanged). Still two parts (far
# under near), still every leg from its joints at the idle's 10 px, 5 px thick; the run legs are now drawn WHOLE so they
# may fold: the capsule of thigh and shin, each pixel cloth (T), knee band (K) or leather (S) by the nearer bone, an
# outline on every silhouette edge, light-left on an upright bone and light-top on a level one (proto2 legkit5.jleg5).
#   Run (contact, pass, flight; bob 1 / 0 / 0; plants 4:-2, -2:-6, -6:-11, holds 6 / 4 / 5, 30 px a cycle): contact run1 /
#   run4, the lead lands flat under a bent knee at +4 (thigh 39 degrees forward, shin upright), the trailing leg pushes off
#   its toe behind (toe-down, toe at +1); pass run2 / run5, the carrying leg straight under the hips (flat at -2), the
#   swing knee driven forward (56 degrees) with the shin folded back under it and its boot toe-down 2 px up at +3, clear
#   in front of the carrying boot; flight run3 / run6, BOTH boots off the ground: the swing knee still up over a flat boot
#   2 px up at +3 (where it lands), the leg that pushed trailing with its boot 1 px up at -6. No leg is ever held out
#   straight in front; the push-off is the toe and the knee, never a longer leg. Poses checked frame by frame against the
#   judge's .tmp/judge/proto2/check.py (its leg length counts the shin it can see above the boot, so a lifted boot costs
#   leg length: the trailing boot lifts 1 px, the swing boot 2).
# History, superseded where it differs by proto2 i2 above:
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTO2 i1 (2026-10-21; the owner's three fixes on prototype i3; supersedes i3 below where they differ).
# TWO PARTS: this part is the NEAR leg (and its boot); legs/adult/loco/far (z -1, drawn first) is the FAR leg, a whole leg
# on its own part, so the far leg is never drawn narrower than the near one: only the pixels the near leg covers hide it.
# EVERY LEG FROM ITS JOINTS: hip, knee, ankle, with the idle's thigh 4.5 (hip -10 to knee -5.5), shin 4 (to the ankle
# inside the boot, -1.5) and foot 1.5 = 10 px; the knee is solved for the hip and the foot (a pose the leg cannot reach
# is refused, never stretched), and the leg is a 5 px thick bone at any angle, cut into the idle's rows (trouser, the knee
# row, the boot shaft over the boot), every row 5 px or more, the far leg's rows at least the near leg's. No folded leg:
# every shin runs down from the knee to the boot. The lead / carrying leg hangs from the forward hip (centre +2, the idle's
# near hip), the trailing / swinging leg from the back hip (-1, the idle's far hip): the pelvis turns as the swing comes
# through, whichever leg is near. The far leg takes the idle's far value (cloth 3 then 2, leather h then g, the first
# visible pixel of each row lit), not one flat dark.
#   Walk (contact, pass, reach; bob 1 / 0 / 0; plants 3:0, 0:-4, -4:-8, 22 px a cycle): contact walkA / walkC, the lead
#   strikes its heel at +3 on a soft knee, the trailing leg on its ball at -8; pass walkA2 / walkC2, the carrying leg
#   straight under the hips (flat at 0), the swing boot just off its toe behind it (toe-down, 2 px up at -8); reach
#   walkB2 / walkD2, the carrying leg straight (flat at -4), the swing leg forward, toe up 1 px at +3.
#   Run (contact, pass, flight; bob 1 / 0 / 0; plants 3:-1, -1:-6, -6:-12, holds 4 / 5 / 6, 30 px a cycle): contact run1 /
#   run4, the lead lands flat on a bent knee at +3, the trailing leg reaches back, its boot 1 px up at -8; pass run2 / run5,
#   the carrying leg straight under the hips (flat at -1), the swing boot kicked up behind it (toe-down, 2 px up at -8), clear
#   of the carrying boot (the narrow frame); flight run3 / run6, both boots off: the leg that pushed lifts off where it stood
#   (flat, 1 px up at -6), the swing leg reaches (toe-up, 1 px up at +4) to land at +3. Push-off is the boot leaving its
#   spot and the knee, never a longer leg; the front leg is forward on two frames of three (reach, land), never held out.
#   The seat row and the elf's extra row are elf-only overlays on far (hidden under every other body's hem).
#   Generated by proto2's legkit4.py / joints.py (scratch) and checked by the judge's .tmp/judge/proto2/check.py.
# History, superseded where it differs by proto2 i1 above:
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTOTYPE i3 (2026-10-21; docs/ref/motion/RESEARCH.md; supersedes i2 below where they differ).
# The same method (per-row shear, 5 px rows, one boot stamp tilted by which pixels touch the ground), new phases:
#   Walk (cycle 20, holds 3, 4, 3): contact walkA / walkC (bob 1), the front leg straight onto a heel strike at +4, the back
#   leg on its ball (toe 0); PASS walkA2 / walkC2 (bob 1), the carrying leg over its flat boot at +1, the swing thigh
#   under it and the shin trailing to a toe-down boot lifted 3 just BEHIND the carrying heel (the boots never overlap: no
#   knot of boots, round i2's pass); REACH walkB2 / walkD2 (bob 0, the highest: Saint11's "up"), the carrying leg slanting
#   back over its flat boot at -3, the swing leg forward over a toe-up boot lifted 1 at +3 (the owner reference's frame
#   4): the swing toe moves +4, +12, +4 px a frame (lift-off, the whip past the carrying leg, the landing) instead of
#   i2's 0, +6, +14 jump into the contact. No down frame (RESEARCH 5.2's eight-frame variant without the down).
#   Run (cycle 30, the planted heel +3 > -1 > -7, holds 4, 6, 5): contact run1 / run4, the front leg landing flat at +3
#   on a bent knee (the thigh forward, the shin upright), the trailing leg kicked back 45 degrees over a toe-down boot
#   lifted 3; RECOVER run2 / run5, the carrying leg under the hips leaning a pixel into the run, the swing knee DRIVEN
#   UP: a horizontal thigh 8-9 px long under the hem, the shin hanging under the knee over a toe-down boot lifted 3 at
#   +3..+9, clear in front of the carrying shin (round i2's knee sat behind the carrying leg: it read as standing);
#   flight run3 / run6 (bob -1), both boots off the ground: the trailing leg back over a blunt toe-down boot lifted 2
#   (round i2's pointed K3 tail), the leading leg's toe-up boot lifted 3. The far leg one flat dark: cloth 2,2,2,
#   leather g (boots_adult's far keys); the near leg lit. Every visible leg row 5 px; the far leg shows 2 px or more
#   where it leaves the near leg. Elves' extra row (the one above the first visible row) is filled to the hip width in
#   the right views as in the left.
#   Generated by the prototype's legkit3.py (scratch) and checked at 12-16x and in motion.
# History, superseded where it differs by prototype i3 above: prototype i2 (2026-10-21):
# (i2) THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTOTYPE i2 (2026-10-21; docs/ref/motion/RESEARCH.md, which supersedes MOTION_P2 5.x's joint
# tables; the owner's docs/ref/motion/owner_walk_ref.png). Every side (R, L) walk and run leg is a column of rows moved per
# row (a shear: never a rotated shape), 5 px a row (outline, 3 px of cloth or leather, outline; 6 at a proud or locked
# knee): 4 trouser rows (the last the knee) over the 3-row boot shaft, the foot ONE boot from maps/stamps/boots_adult.stamps
# (K0 flat, or split by `cols` into a 1-row tilt: heel strike HS, heel off HO, toe down TD when lifted; K3 pointed in the
# run's flight). A lifted leg is shorter (fewer thigh rows), never squashed. THE VALUES CARRY THE LEGS: the near leg is lit
# (cloth 4,3,3 / leather i,i,h), the far leg one flat dark (cloth 2,2,2 / leather h,g,g), drawn first, one outline where
# they meet, so the contact frames 0 and 3 read as two different legs (round i1's 3,2,2 far leg read as the same leg).
#   Walk (cycle 20, the planted heel +4 > +1 > -3 > -6, holds 3, 4, 3: RESEARCH 5.2's own rule, frames at 83 ms or slower at
#   40 px/s, and the contact stride opens a 3 px gap between the feet): contact walkA / walkC, the front leg straight onto a
#   heel strike at +4, the back leg bent at the boot top on its ball (toe -1); down walkA2 / walkC2 (bob 1), the front boot
#   flat at +1 under a proud knee, the back leg trailing on its ball (toe -3); pass walkB2 / walkD2, the carrying leg upright
#   over its flat boot at -3 (the knee locked a pixel proud), the swing leg's knee a pixel ahead of it and its shin trailing
#   to a toe-down boot lifted 2 BEHIND the carrying ankle (the reference's frame 3), where it shows.
