# History, superseded for the side walk and run by prototype i2 above: prototype i1 (2026-10-21):
# (i1) THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTOTYPE i1 (2026-10-21; docs/ref/motion/RESEARCH.md, which supersedes MOTION_P2 5.x's joint
# tables; the owner's docs/ref/motion/owner_walk_ref.png: "the feet art constantly flat but can be angled throughout the
# strides"). Every side (R, L) walk and run leg is a 5 px column of rows (outline, 3 px of cloth or leather, outline; 6 at a
# bent knee) moved per row (a shear: never a rotated shape), 4 trouser rows (the last the knee) over the 3-row boot shaft,
# the foot ONE boot from maps/stamps/boots_adult.stamps: K0 flat, or K0 split by `cols` into a 1-row tilt (heel strike:
# the toe cols 4-6 a row up; heel off: the heel cols 0-2 a row up, the ball down; toe down when lifted: cols 0-3 a row
# above cols 4-6), K1 toe-up and K3 pointed for the run's flight. The shaft and boot are one shape: a tilt is which foot
# pixels touch the ground. The far leg is drawn first, a value darker (cloth 3,2,2 / leather h,h,g against the near leg's
# 4,3,2 / i,i,h), one outline where the legs meet; its lifted boot shows. A lifted leg is shorter (fewer thigh rows).
#   Walk (cycle 16; the planted heel +2 > 0 > -3 > -6, steps 2, 3, 3; loco.clip): contact walkA / walkC, the front leg
#   sheared forward 2 onto a heel strike at +2, the back leg sheared back 2 on its ball (toe 0); down walkA2 / walkC2
#   (bob 1), the front boot flat at 0, the back leg sheared back 4 on its ball with the toe where it stood (-2): both feet
#   down, the widest frame (the reference's frame 2); pass walkB2 / walkD2, the carrying leg upright over its flat boot at
#   -3, the swing leg through in front of it, the knee a pixel forward, its boot lifted toe down (toe +6, heel 2 rows up).
#   The thighs' tops slide with the stride (near: 0, -1, -3, -4, -4, 0), never a square wave; the hip row stays 7-9 px.
#   Run (cycle 30; the planted heel +4 > 0 > -5; holds 4, 5, 6: the long one airborne): contact run1 / run4, the front leg
#   straight, sheared 4 onto a flat landing at +4, the trailing leg folding under (boot lifted 2, toe down, toe 0);
#   recover run2 / run5, the carrying leg under the hips (a bent knee a pixel proud), the swing knee driven forward, its
#   boot lifted 2 toe down ahead (toe +9); flight run3 / run6 (bob -1), both boots 2 rows clear: the pushing leg 45 degrees
#   back on a pointed K3 (toe -2), the leading knee up over a toe-up K1 (heel +3). Never wider than 45 degrees.
#   Her `when woman replace` views: the same placements, the back-most leg a pixel fuller on its two top rows. The left
#   views: the right views' rows mirrored (x' = -x - 1) and re-shaded left-lit, the hips 2 px fuller at the back on the 3
#   rows from the first visible one (A3's left idle: hip row 10 against the right view's 8), an elf's overlay carrying the
#   same on the row above. Generated from per-row spans by the prototype's legkit.py (the artist's authoring aid, scratch)
#   and checked at 8-16x and in motion. B11's and B12's MOTION_P2 table checks (feet keys, stance, pass shape, span
#   envelope, stamp shapes) are superseded for these keys; B11's mass checks (area, hip row, leg runs) hold.
# History, superseded for the side walk and run by prototype i1 above: the motion rebuild (2026-10-21, MOTION_P2):
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, the motion rebuild (2026-10-21; docs/MOTION_P2.md, STYLE_P2 10 "The owner's motion reference";
# the owner's docs/ref/motion/owner_walk_ref.png: "the feet art constantly flat but can be angled throughout the
# strides"). Every side (R, L) walk and run key is two continuous limbs, hip > thigh > knee > shin > boot: the trouser
# thigh from the seat, the knee on the last trouser row (a bent knee a corner 1-2 px out from the shin under it), the
# leather shaft as the shin, the foot on it at a clean ankle. The foot is ONE boot in hand-drawn tilts of A3's idle foot
# (maps/stamps/boots_adult.stamps, placed by `put`, which pxc expands; `tags boots-stamped` refuses a hand-drawn boot
# pixel): K0 flat, K1 toe-up (runs 3,2,2; its top outline closed over the instep), K2 heel-off (runs 2,2,3: on its
# ball), K3 toe-off 1:2 (the lifted and pointed foot); near and far tones; the L keys mirrored and re-lit. K4 (the 45
# degree hang) is no longer placed: a 45 degree turn of the 20 px boot reads as a stick. A shin's last row covers at most
# 1 px of its own tilted key (the heel top), the stamp's outline its back edge.
#   Walk (cycle 18; plants = the planted heel 3:0, 0:-3, -3:-6): contact walkA / walkC, the front leg reaching into a
#   toe-up K1 on its heel at +3 (the shin's front edge running into the top of the foot), the back leg leaning back onto
#   a K2 on its ball at 0, the heel two rows up, the legs apart from F-6; down walkA2 / walkC2 (bob 1), the front K0
#   planted at 0 under the hips, its knee a pixel proud, the trailing thigh down from the hip a pixel a row to the knee
#   on F-6, the shin 2 px back from its corner onto a K3 rolled onto its toe at -3 (where it stood); pass walkB2 / walkD2
#   (fix r3, the reference's frame 3), one straight leg over its K0 at -3 carrying the body, the other lifted BEHIND it:
#   the thighs one run from the hip, the swing knee on F-7 behind the planted knee, its shin stepping back from the
#   knee's corner (the back of the knee open at u -3, F-6), its K3 toe down at -5 lifted 1 with a column of daylight
#   (u -4) between the two boots (walkD2's near swing drawn over the far planted thigh). Where the thighs meet, one
#   outline (the near leg's) divides them, never two.
#   Run (cycle 36; plants 3:-2, -2:-7, -7:-15; every visible trouser pixel the knee region): contact run1 / run4, a flat
#   K0 landing at +3 under a bent knee, behind it the trailing leg in recovery: the thigh back to the knee on F-7, the
#   shin straight down one row, the K3 pointed toe down at -3, 2 rows clear (the ankle about 80 degrees); push run2 /
#   run5, the planted leg under the hips over its K0 at -2, the swing knee driven forward (6 px ahead of the planted
#   shin) and its K3 toe down under it, 2 rows clear (toe +9); flight run3 / run6 (bob -1), both boots 2 rows clear, the
#   leading knee up and its shin hanging over a K0 above the landing spot (+3), the trailing leg just pushed off: the
#   thigh a pixel a row back to the knee on F-7, the shin 2 px back from its corner, the K3 pointed at its end (toe -4).
#   Never a stiff inverted V.
#   The hem rides a row up (the garments' side `run` views, loco.clip torso=run); the seat (the drawing's top row, under
#   the hem; elves show it) spans the first visible row. Her `when woman replace` views: the same placements, her hips a
#   pixel fuller at the back (not the pass's seat, which already reaches u -4: a leaning elder's hem bares none), her
#   ankle a pixel in on the side that keeps the edge a 1 px staircase into the key under it (in front over a K0 or a
#   K2; behind over a K1 heel, a taper; a row up on a trailing K3 leg; none on a lifted swing or kicked shin). The left
#   views: the right views' rows mirrored (x' = -x - 1), every leg stretch re-lit for the top-left light (its outline
#   pixels where the mirror puts them, its shading light-left again), the hips a pixel fuller at the back on the first
#   two visible rows (A3's left idle: the L hip row 9-11 px), with a `when elf` overlay carrying an elf's seat a pixel
#   past the base seat behind. Drawn with the fix-r3 authoring aid (every row hand-placed in the R man's views; the
#   woman's and L views derived by those rules and checked at 8-16x).
#   B11 limbs and B12 boots (rpg_test --doll --gates) and the harness's J2 trace (.tmp/judge/motion) measure them.
# History, superseded for the side walk and run by the rebuild above (front and back keys, the idles, `stance`, `lunge`,
# `buckle`, `sit`, `lie` and `guard` are unchanged):
# The walk and run keys were redrawn 2026-10-19 for the owner, twice. Round 1 ("his legs all of a sudden get super
# skinny"): every leg keeps the idle's mass in every frame, the seat a solid block under the hem, the back leg a value
# darker, never thinner. Round 2 ("the feet are getting rotated, joints look a little off"): every boot is A3's idle
# boot moved and lifted, never redrawn at an angle (the planted one flat on row F, its 7 px sole centred on the clip's
# plant anchor); the legs are upright trouser blocks that bend at the knee (one step at the knee, the boot top under
# it), no staircase legs; a compact stride. Side views: contact walkA / walkC, down walkA2 / walkC2 (bob 1: the planted
# knee bent over its boot, the other boot lifted 1 behind), pass walkB2 / walkD2 (bob -1: the swing knee ahead, its boot
# lifted 2 under it). The left views are the right
# views' shapes mirrored, each run re-lit from the left, a pixel forward. Front and back: walkA / walkC a foot landing
# (lifted 1), walkA2 / walkC2 both feet down, walkB / walkD the swing foot lifted 2. `when woman replace` views are
# her own legs: the same feet (one walk table), her hips and upper thighs a pixel fuller, her boots fitted (the shaft a
# pixel slimmer, the ankle in), so her legs taper bare too. The regions (T thigh, K knee, S shin, B boot, O sole) let a
# look show bare legs. `stance` is A3's own side contact legs, kept pixel for pixel for the sword swing
# (clips/actions/sword.clip). B11 (rpg_test --doll --gates) holds the mass.
# The side run, round 4 (2026-10-20, the owner circled it: "the feet are completely disconnected from the body"):
# the old keys set the back boot 3-4 px behind its thigh, joined to the hem by one trouser row. Round 5 (the leg pass)
# joined every boot to a trouser stub, but under the F-9 hem the legs stayed a 2-3 row trouser block on two boots that
# touched ("a short dark strip", "a torso sitting on a pair of boots"). Round 6 (the leg pass, round 2, 2026-10-20):
# the hem rides a row up in the side run (every torso-keyed garment's side `run` view, the clip's torso=run; the
# knee-length skirts' flare views kick up to the same hem, F-10, F-11 in flight), and every side run leg is redrawn
# as a LIMB from the seat (one solid row under the hem, the elf's hip row above it) to its boot: three or four trouser
# rows on the planted or trailing leg, two on a raised one, the two legs split by background from the first row under
# the seat (gapLL 6-11), angled from the hip by one 1 px step a row, the trouser a pixel wider at the knee over a
# planted boot. Every boot is A3's idle boot moved and lifted, never rotated; a compact stride: 13 px heel to toe at
# contact, no heel more than 5 px behind the pivot. Contact run1 / run4: the planted leg reaching (its sole centred on
# the plant anchor, +5), the trailing boot on its toe (lifted 1, its heel at -4), its thigh angled back from the seat.
# Push run2 / run5: the planted leg straight under the hips (0); the swing leg passing, its knee through and its boot
# lifted 2 in front, where it will land. Flight run3 / run6 (bob -1): the pushing leg trailing a 1 px step a row back
# from the seat (lifted 1, its heel at -5), the leading knee up, its boot lifted 3 over the landing spot (it lands
# straight down into the next contact). The keys come from the leg placements (trouser span per row, boot heel, lift)
# in the right view; the left views mirror them a pixel forward (x' = -x - 1) with every string kept left-lit (re-lit
# from the left); her `when woman replace` views are the same placements with her fuller back on the first visible
# row and her ankle in. The seat's back corner sits a pixel in from the far hand where it hangs behind the hip (right
# view, run3 / run4); in the left view the seat matches the idle's hips, and the push frames' passing thigh is a pixel
# fuller in front, where the near fist hangs over it. Every visible run trouser pixel is the knee region (a kilt's bare
# leg under the flared skirt).
# Round 7 (the leg pass, round 3, 2026-10-20): in push and flight the second leg was still a boot glued under the hem
# or hung on the planted leg (one row of its own). Now every boot has two or more rows of its own leg below the seat
# and the two legs are apart by background in every row below the seat down to the boots (the push frames' feet meet
# only where the planted toe tucks over the raised heel on F-2 / F-1). Push run2 / run5: the swing leg passes IN FRONT
# of the planted one, its 5 px thigh angled forward from the seat (one 1 px step a row) to the knee, the boot (the
# shin) straight under it, lifted 1, its heel at +3 (13 px heel to toe; +4 put the toe past the frame's edge and the
# armed elf's RUN atlas over B10's 64 KB); the planted leg holds the idle's back edge for two rows under the seat, then
# steps in at the knee. Flight run3 / run6: the leading boot lifted 2 (3 left it one row), its heel at +3, clear of the
# trailing boot (15 px heel to toe), its thigh a 1 px step a row forward from the seat. Contact unchanged. Her fuller
# back never sits past the run hem's back edge in the right view (-4).
use person
body adult
role legs std
layer legs
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_adult
tags boots-stamped

